$$
\quad \mathbf{u}\cdot\mathbf{v} = \underbrace{u_1 \cdot v_1 + u_2 \cdot v_2 + \cdots + u_n \cdot v_n}_{\Large{n} \,\textrm{-terms}} = \sum_{i=1}^n u_i v_i.
$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "a465d6d9-270d-5cd3-98c8-a78c527b3558" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3183 :tutorial/title "General Rules"} {:db/id 17592186120670 :step/content {:db/id 17592186119803 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186119614 :question/id #uuid "ba38ff28-b4f3-59b8-b18a-a278db26294d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4784"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec386a91-fc52-56d8-8531-7e78a8464380" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048954}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186120308} {:db/id 17592186120373} {:db/id 17592186240979} {:db/id 17592186317166} {:db/id 17592186342112} {:db/id 17592186342113} {:db/id 17592186364351}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Dot Product of Two Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "4acc22bf-58df-50bc-b180-3077f975037c" :step/math-academy-id 17450 :step/next {:db/id 17592186120671}} {:db/id 17592186120671 :step/content {:db/id 17592186119804 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186119615 :question/id #uuid "3ec5f9d5-327b-59e5-8df7-fb37d4054021" :question/math-academy-id "e-4785"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94f8e0e5-8d8a-516a-8f46-d76e94305df4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048774} {:db/id 17592186048963} {:db/id 17592186050465}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186120372} {:db/id 17592186120376} {:db/id 17592186240980} {:db/id 17592186240981} {:db/id 17592186240982} {:db/id 17592186317169} {:db/id 17592186342114} {:db/id 17592186342115} {:db/id 17592186366822} {:db/id 17592186368723}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Quantity in an Expression Involving the Dot Product"} :step/id #uuid "36416450-4cfa-51cd-be65-4dead60ba52e" :step/math-academy-id 17451} {:db/id 17592186121062 :tutorial/content "To add two vectors in $\mathbb{R}^n,$ we just need to add their corresponding components. To illustrate, consider the vectors $\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b} \in \mathbb{R}^4,$ given by

$$
[\begin{aligned}5 \\ 1 \\ -3 \\ 6\end{aligned}]
$$

To compute $\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b},$ all we have to do is to add each component of the vector $\mathbf{a}$ with the corresponding component of $\mathbf{b}.$ Doing this, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\begin{aligned}5 \\ 1 \\ -3 \\ 6\end{aligned}]+[\begin{aligned}-5 \\ 3 \\ 1 \\ 0\end{aligned}] \\  & =[\begin{aligned}5+(-5) \\ 1+3 \\ -3+1 \\ 6+0\end{aligned}] \\  & =[\begin{aligned}0 \\ 4 \\ -2 \\ 6\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$

We can only compute the sum, difference, or dot product of two vectors if both vectors have the same number of components. For example, we can't find the following sum, so we say it's *undefined*:

$$
[\begin{aligned}1 \\ 2 \\ 3\end{aligned}]
$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "34cc8b84-ed7a-54e2-995c-12a2b57b0ff0" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3922 :tutorial/title "Adding Two Vectors"} {:db/id 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} {:course/id #uuid "1ee987ec-c9ff-5d2f-91f4-4de8079c0eac" :course/math-academy-id 145 :db/id 17592186046658}] "attributes" [[10 :db/ident :db.type/keyword :db.cardinality/one] [11 :db.install/partition :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [13 :db.install/attribute :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [15 :db/excise :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/one] [16 :db.excise/attrs :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [17 :db.excise/beforeT :db.type/long :db.cardinality/one] [18 :db.excise/before :db.type/instant :db.cardinality/one] [19 :db.alter/attribute :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [40 :db/valueType :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/one] [41 :db/cardinality :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/one] [42 :db/unique :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/one] [43 :db/isComponent :db.type/boolean :db.cardinality/one] [44 :db/index :db.type/boolean :db.cardinality/one] [45 :db/noHistory :db.type/boolean :db.cardinality/one] [50 :db/txInstant :db.type/instant :db.cardinality/one] [51 :db/fulltext :db.type/boolean :db.cardinality/one] [52 :db/fn :db.type/fn :db.cardinality/one] [62 :db/doc :db.type/string :db.cardinality/one] [65 :db/tupleType :db.type/keyword :db.cardinality/one] [66 :db/tupleTypes :db.type/tuple :db.cardinality/one] [67 :db/tupleAttrs :db.type/tuple :db.cardinality/one] [68 :db/ensure :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [69 :db.entity/attrs :db.type/keyword :db.cardinality/many] [70 :db.entity/preds :db.type/symbol :db.cardinality/many] [71 :db.attr/preds :db.type/symbol :db.cardinality/many] [72 :db.tuple/discontinued :db.type/boolean :db.cardinality/one] [1000 :course-group/courses :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [1001 :course-group/title :db.type/string :db.cardinality/one] [1002 :course-group/id :db.type/uuid :db.cardinality/one] [1003 :course/next :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [1004 :course/